From 32931b948dbf57de9b0506c3064dea66a8df3ce5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:27:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: dptx: widen DPTX_CONNECT_TIMEOUT to 8s as a
 diagnostic

Direct follow-up to 0129: widening set_hpd's own timeout there confirmed
DCP really was sending a valid, slower-than-1s reply that the host was
cutting off -- but the failure just moved one step later, to this
existing 2000ms wait_for_completion_timeout(linkcfg_completion, ...).
Every dcpext1 attempt since (0128 x2, 0129 x2) shows the identical
pattern: request_display succeeds, then ~5s of silence, then DCP sends
DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING/DEVICE_NOT_STARTED on its own, then this
completion times out with no SET_LINK_RATE/WILL_CHANGE_LINK_CONFIG burst
ever appearing (unlike 0127, where that burst fired instantly and DCP
reached DPRX_DONE=1).

Same single-variable logic as 0129: widen only this one wait to 8s and
see whether the link-training burst is also just running late, or
whether it genuinely never comes on this pipeline/port regardless of
patience -- which would point away from timeouts entirely and toward
whatever DCP's firmware actually decided during that silent window.

dcp->hpd_mutex is already released before this wait begins (dcp.c:1470,
unchanged), so unlike 0129 this change adds no additional lock-hold time
at all. Single macro value changed; the only other reference
(the dev_dbg elapsed-time print) is unaffected in behavior. Full
reasoning in notes/2026-09-24-0130-widen-linkcfg-timeout-diagnostic.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 0fe8c5f..dc64c1e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -1376,7 +1376,17 @@ bool dcp_has_typec_routes(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return dcp->nr_typec_routes;
 }
 
-#define DPTX_CONNECT_TIMEOUT msecs_to_jiffies(2000)
+/*
+ * Diagnostic (candidate 0130, see notes/2026-09-24-0130-*.md): widening
+ * set_hpd's own timeout in 0129 confirmed a real, slower DCP reply was
+ * being cut off there -- the failure just moved to this next wait
+ * instead (DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING/DEVICE_NOT_STARTED fire, then this
+ * completion times out with no SET_LINK_RATE/WILL_CHANGE_LINK_CONFIG
+ * burst at all). Widening this one too, same single-variable logic,
+ * to see whether that burst is also just running late or genuinely
+ * never coming on this pipeline/port regardless of patience.
+ */
+#define DPTX_CONNECT_TIMEOUT msecs_to_jiffies(8000)
 #define DPTX_RECONNECT_DELAY msecs_to_jiffies(1000)
 #define DPTX_RECONNECT_RETRIES 1
 
-- 
